# Focus management

- Prefer semantic buttons, links, and form controls. Do not add redundant tab stops to native controls.
- Use only `tabIndex={0}` or `tabIndex={-1}` when necessary; never positive values to reorder focus.
- Reuse `packages/web/src/shared/lib/focus.ts` and existing dialog/menu primitives. Preserve focus trapping, Escape handling, and focus return to the trigger.
- Custom composite controls need a coherent keyboard model, visible focus, and accessible names; clickable `div` elements do not supply these automatically.
- Avoid autofocus that steals focus during background updates. Verify keyboard navigation and disabled/hidden states for the changed flow.
